        <body>
            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0260" n="164" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg164"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Storer to Mr. Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 141.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    regulations of the importation of fresh, salted, and preserved meats into
                    Belgium has been again amended. I beg to refer to my dispatch No. 83, dated
                    January 27, 1898, for a statement of the substance of the amendment of these
                    regulations, then just made, stating the impossibility at that time of
                    forwarding a printed copy. I beg now to inclose a reprinted copy of the said
                    “arrete” or decree of December 14, 1897, amending the law as then existing and
                    of which the Department was already in possession, and also an abstract of the
                    “Moniteur Belge” of August 29 and 30, 1898, containing the amendments last made,
                    dated August 22, 1898.</p>
                <p>It will be observed that now the inspection and conditions of importation are
                    extended to include “fats and extracts produced from cattle, sheep, goats, and
                    hogs;” that the importation of fats and extracts of horse flesh, as well as the
                    flesh itself, are prohibited, and that the stamp of inspection may be placed on
                    the case or cover of the package in case of preserved or tinned meats.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bellamy Storer.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>






